sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch02-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because the dominant species of larger genera vary most and varieties become new species, larger genera tend to become larger, and dominant forms tend to become more dominant by leaving many modified, dominant descendants.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Larger genera tend to grow larger and dominant forms more dominant";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter II, “Variation under Nature”; section “Summary”. Scope: genera and dominant species throughout nature"
}
